00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.250
MARIANA VAN ZELLER:
[speaking spanish]

00:01:57.317 --> 00:02:00.453
CARTEL MEMBER:
[speaking spanish]

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:16.302
MARIANA VAN ZELLER:
[speaking spanish]

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.471
CARTEL MEMBER:
[speaking spanish]

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:19.639
MARIANA VAN ZELLER: A month.

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:20.840
[speaking spanish]

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.976
CARTEL MEMBER:
[speaking spanish]

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:26.012
MARIANA VAN ZELLER:
[speaking spanish]

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:29.182
CARTEL MEMBER:
[speaking spanish]

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.617
MARIANA VAN ZELLER:
50 calibers, RPGs.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.551
[speaking spanish]

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:36.389
CARTEL MEMBER:
[speaking spanish]

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:38.191
MARIANA VAN ZELLER: None
of this sounds like arming

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:40.326
a criminal organization.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:43.129
They're arming for war.

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:50.036
[speaking spanish]

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:56.843
CARTEL MEMBER:
[speaking spanish]

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.411
[upbeat music]

00:02:58.478 --> 00:02:59.913
MARIANA VAN ZELLER:
I'm told the buyer is

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.248
from an affiliated
cartel fighting

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.817
to regain territory in Sonora.

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:09.856
He's picking up a fresh order,
including a pair of customized

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:14.260
handguns for rich narcos who
don't just want a weapon,

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:17.463
they want to make a statement.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.600
Sales like this are common
for these smugglers.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:24.137
The market for American
assault rifles is exploding.

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.573
CARTEL MEMBER:
[speaking spanish]

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.942
MARIANA VAN ZELLER:
[speaking spanish]

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.610
CARTEL MEMBER:
[speaking spanish]

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:34.213
MARIANA VAN ZELLER: [bleep]
So they had 200 AK-47s

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.382
[speaking spanish] which is
what they call them here,

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:39.586
come through here, San Felipe,
in just one day last week.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.221
[speaking spanish]

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:45.692
CARTEL MEMBER:
[speaking spanish]

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.494
MARIANA VAN ZELLER: Here's
where things get interesting.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.830
Remember when I said
that you never ask

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.999
what cartel someone belongs to?

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:54.467
I didn't.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:57.203
This guy just decided to
tell me that he works for one

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:00.373
of the fastest growing
mafias in Mexico, the Jalisco

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.876
Cartel, also known as CJNG.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.511
MAN: [speaking spanish]

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.547
MARIANA VAN ZELLER: The
organization is only about 10

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:10.083
years old, but
aggressive maneuvers

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:13.286
and terrifying
ISIS-style executions

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:15.054
have helped them
dominate underworld

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:18.358
markets across Mexico,
becoming the Sinaloa

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:22.195
Cartel's biggest rival.

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:24.697
And the kingpin of
these violent upstarts,

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:28.034
perhaps the most dangerous
drug lord in the world,

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.570
is known as El Mencho.

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:34.173
CARTEL MEMBER:
[speaking spanish]

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.342
MARIANA VAN ZELLER:
[speaking spanish]

